            <ArticleTitle>L5 radicular pain related to lumbar extradural gas-containing pseudocyst. Role of CT-guided aspiration.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>552-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>L5 radicular pain related to an epidural gas-containing pseudocyst is described in a 62-year-old female. Transient resolution of radicular pain was observed after CT-guided gas aspiration. Recurrent radicular pain led to surgical treatment; after operation the radicular pain disappeared.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
